Package: homelab-accountmanage
Architecture: all
Depends: perl (>= 5.36),
         homelab-common,
         libmojolicious-perl,
         libyaml-libyaml-perl,
         adduser
Recommends: homelab-api, homelab-sso, homelab-agent
Description: Account self-service + administration web UI for the homelab-* ecosystem
 A thin BFF Mojolicious app served at myaccount.<domain>: browsers talk
 only to this app, which delegates login to homelab-sso (OAuth2
 authorization-code, via Homelab::Common::SSOClient) and then aggregates
 read/write calls to the existing services -- homelab-api for account
 info, sessions and password, homelab-drive for storage usage -- using
 the logged-in user's own token. It owns no database of its own; every
 panel it renders is gated by what that token is actually allowed to do,
 so the same app is self-service for a regular user and administration
 for a site_admin. Registers itself in homelab-api's service registry.
